// Title: Suspicious Execution of InstallUtil Without Log
// Sigma ID: d042284c-a296-4988-9be5-f424fadcc28c
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2022-01-23 | Modified: 2022-02-04
// ATT&CK: stealth
// Description: Uses the .NET InstallUtil.exe application in order to execute image without log
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://securelist.com/moonbounce-the-dark-side-of-uefi-firmware/105468/
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/framework/tools/installutil-exe-installer-tool
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_instalutil_no_log_execution.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\InstallUtil.exe" and FolderPath contains "Microsoft.NET\\Framework" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "/logfile= " and ProcessCommandLine contains "/LogToConsole=false")
